guest(i386nt) kernel driver which was written by LLM partialy(but i dominated the key part of procedure)


compiation:
  cd /path/to/ntivshmem/src/.../driver
  ensure that you've installed clang(LLVM)
  ./compile2.sh compiles out a .sys file
  the correnpondent INF desc file in the same dir
  copy them to WindowsXP(put on the same dir)
  go to device manager,install the inf,the device name usually named "PCI standard RAM controller"


